  "build_statement": "All seven images in this lock were built fresh (subject-origin fresh_build) on GitHub-hosted runners by the forced workflow_dispatch agent-platform-images run 40399370888 for S, with seven successful jobs and headSha == S. The automatic workflow_run 40399304267 for the same S selected no image (only a test changed since the previous build). All seven digests were verified with the repository verifier: agent_platform.release_verify Verifier.signature and Verifier.attestation, and scripts/image-provenance.py --verify-ref (Verifier.provenance). History: for the previous S e34d716 the forced run 40387775479 failed only at the duplicate KMS attestation and the automatic run 40387719937 built all seven; that lock was never opened because test_demo_check read the committed lock (fixed in #175).",
  "known_defect": "agent-platform-images.yml existing-tag path: it calls gcloud beta container binauthz attestations sign-and-create although an attestation for that digest already exists, so a forced run after a successful run for the same S fails with a conflict. Fix after the release, then also record it in docs/security/known-limitations.md.",
